If you will accept a probabilitic approach [i.e. you can do this indefiniately
with high probability], then you could also just do the extinctionist thing,
then go live on your quest level forever- since extinction doesnt apply to
the quest level monsters, an unbounded number of them can get created- doing
this before killing Rodney [probably the better idea] gives a 1/70 chance
that a monster will be created on any given turn- assuming a ring of slow
digestion and some amulet, and for simplicity that you are a valkyrie (the
calculations could be repeated for other classes with appropriate monster
types)- the probability that your nutrition drops by more than 750 before
you can eat a fire giant [fire ants provide little nutrition, so i skip them
in the my calculations- they simply make you more likely to find food]: 

on any turn, there is a 1/70 chance of a call to makemon.
since everything is extinct, there is a 6/7 chance of a monster getting
created [i.e. a call to qt_mon]- this means a 6/490 chance of getting
a monster on a turn. There is a 1/5 chance of the "type 1" monster getting
created and a 4/5 chance of the "type 2" monster getting created- Im
pretty sure, but cant find where to confirm right off that fire giants
are the type 1 monster [and if they are type 2, you are 4 times as likely
to get food]. So that gives a 6/2450 = 3/1225 chance of a fire giant
being created on any turn.  With a ring of slow digestion and an amulet,
750 nutrition is consumed in 7500 turns. So the chances of not finding
a fire giant in that time are (1222/1225)^7500= 1.031E -8.  If you were
pretty well satiated from previous fire giant snacks, you can probably
go twice as long before you start to get into trouble- (1222/1225)^(7500*2) is
1.06 E -16. Compare this to the chances of finding at least two fire giants
in the 7500 turn window [and thereby being able to significantly increase
your nutrition above where it started]- would be 1-P(0 giants)-P(1 giant)=
99.9999799802%

Therefore, with high probability, your game lasts forever.
